<article class="env-lemma" id="0EXM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EXM">Lemma <span data-tag="0EXM">9.21.5</span>.</a> Let $L/K$ be a finite separable extension of fields. Let $M$ be the normal closure of $L$ over $K$ (Definition <a href="/tag/0BMF" data-tag="0BMF">9.16.4</a>). Then $M/K$ is Galois. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The subextension $M/M_{sep}/K$ of Lemma <a href="/tag/030K" data-tag="030K">9.14.6</a> is normal by Lemma <a href="/tag/0EXK" data-tag="0EXK">9.15.4</a>. Since $L/K$ is separable we have $L \subset M_{sep}$. By minimality $M = M_{sep}$ and the proof is done. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>